od if you want to learn about the prophet peace be upon him in his life you would be interested in the details right um the other issue is they a lot of them don't provide proper referencing footnotes and a lot of them don't provide a variety when it comes to the works that they're quoting now in regards to the sealed nectar the reason why it's easily the most popular book at least in the english language is", "because the author of the sealed nectar won an award in the 70s i believe no doubt concealed nectar is a book of great value and praiseworthy work on the life of muhammad peace be upon him this book has been written by the eminent shaykh of germa yes india the first islamic conference on syrah was held in 1976 in pakistan sponsored by the world by the muslim world league the manuscript of sheikh safir rahman in barak puri salafi banaras author of the book in hand received the first grand prize of fifty thousand saudi arabs for its authentic and sad and sound collections of the narrations right so um the book won an award in 1976 and due to that for the longest time it's been seen as the best book of syra but it has been 50 years and you'd expect something in the past 50 years to", "surpass it right but technically the best book of sira is a traditional source and it's simply due to the amount of details in that book however however i would only recommend certain for those that know the arabic language and for those that have the ability to study the chains of narrations of each and every single report which is i mean not the simplest of tasks and yeah so i wouldn't recommend it to the average reader but what i would recommend is media restaurants a biography of the prophetess of islam for several reasons also it's by the way it's in two volumes around 900 pages um and it does it takes all the right boxes it's heavily referenced as you can see here below in the footnotes and of course that's where this book shines because the author not only relies on ibn but 