#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("It's an excellent question And the answer to that question is we have to look at the person giving the da'wah Are you qualified to give the dawah or not is the first question that we need to ask, right? Because dawah can be given in different ways, can be given with your behaviour: Akhlaq (character) as a Muslim, giving your neighbor a gift, being nice to them, helping them, removing obstacles from the road, or doing these things that when people see you, it becomes a source of dawah As you see many, many people accepting Islam because of the behaviour they see of the Muslims They mention, oh, I've seen them, how they behave, they're good, they're nice, they're strict upon what they believe, they do good things This is dawah within itself And other forms of dawah is direct dawah, just directly speak to the person So if you want to do direct dawah, where you directly speak to the person,", "then we see if you're qualified, meaning you have the foundation, the fundamentals of the Faith, understanding the أصول the foundational principles in this religion, and that whatever you say, you speak what you know, and you leave that which you do not know that's the first thing Now, many people who don't have these skills, how do we do dawah to our people around us? Very simple Purchase a copy of the Quran and give it to them There's nothing easier than this Purchase a copy of the Quran, give it to your neighbour, give it to the co-worker, give it to your friend, and say to them, if you have any questions later, you can ask me They bring questions, say to them, I'll come back to you with the answer Ask a person of knowledge, get the answers, give it back to them Anyone is able to do this", "There isn't someone who is not able to do this Say, that's a great question If you don't know the answer, if it's not as simple as like how many prayers do you pray a day, if it's something more difficult, go to someone of knowledge, get the information, get the answers, and come back and give them the answers But giving them the Quran is a huge step along the way And your behaviour and manners with them is a huge step along the way Of course, we know that, I heard that there are not many dawah tables here, for example I heard that there are not many dawah tables here, we need to change this There are people sitting down here today, right?", "This lecture, unfortunately, you didn't come with your swords today; no pens and no papers. So you should come with your swords So if you had your swords and you wrote down the information, InshaAllah, it's available, and recorded Lucky for you, as they say, where you can record the information later If you have this information, you just go to the dawah table and just present it You just sit at the dawah table and give free Quran It's enough to establish the Truth with these people Without argumentation, without many back and forth, just presenting this information, leading them to people of knowledge If they have questions you don't know, you go seek the answers We need to establish this here How many people are sitting down here?", "Tens of people are sitting here Why are we not able to go and set up a dawah stall? Why are we not able to do this? Brothers, do you have legs here? Are you able to walk? I just want to confirm If you don't, then OK, we can talk about something else But you got legs, you walk, you go to work, you come back from work And there are some brothers who are doing it Why are we not doing more? Why are we not doing it in more locations, different locations? It's to be done And as we said, just speak what you know If you don't feel like you're a person of knowledge, set up the stall.", "Seek knowledge every day as it's an obligation of every Muslim and give the Quran to the people And you have have done your effort And our brother from the Deen Show, Deen Center, you guys are welcome to connect with them I'm sure they'll help you seek knowledge as well with the dawah, material, these things you require from them We're more than happy to help you, but we need to establish this more I want to come next time, InshaAllah, if Allah gives me life and I'm able to come, if I came here, I'll say: how many dawah tables?", "You guys, everyone lift their hands, Hands up, and I'm: oh, MashaAllah! (God has willed it!) InshaAllah, we need to do that. Put that intention. And know this is for your goodness This is for your goodness, for your آخرة (Akhira: Hereafter) before it is for anyone else. OK?",))
