#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("No, no, I get what you're saying No, no. It's a general question. We're speaking in general So generally speaking, there are certain people that certain methods work with them, and there are certain people where only guidance is from God So for instance, Prophet Muhammadﷺ was better than any of us in conveying the Message, but his uncle.. for instance, he was trying to convey the Message to him. He was conveying the Message to him, not trying He was doing it. But then he died rejecting it. And then Allahﷻ revealed to him that (You do not guide the ones you choose, Allah is The One Who chooses to guide) [alQasas28:56] It's in the heart.", "The hearts are in the Hands of God. I can try my best, but Allah gives us examples of the uncles of the Prophetﷺ, etc. not being believers, Being among the enemies his whole life. So you can understand that guidance is from God, from Allahﷻ And this life is a test. But also a very important thing is this, you could bring someone other than yourself Maybe someone else would respect, someone else, would listen to, more than you You can bring someone that they don't know Maybe they would be willing to have a discussion with them more than they would with their own son So with their own son, they'd be like, you know what, yesterday I was teaching you, – Now you want to tell me what I should believe",))
