#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("No no, I'll tell you, ignore everything you heard from these people. This is the problem! The Prophetﷺ mentioned, Wallahi (I swear by God) he told us as Muslims! He said: إنَّ مِنكُم مُنَفِّرِينَ (from among you, people who are repellers) You repel people away from the Truth, you repel people away from goodness Even if their intention is good, they're doing it the wrong way. They're pushing people away from the religion, pushing people away from the Truth You will have to miss prayers when you accept Islam, because you still haven't learned how to pray. And that's not a Major Sin, you know!", "Because you still got to learn how to pray first. Look, these people don't have the experience, don't have the understanding of Prophet Muhammadﷺ This is what you learn FROM THE PROPHET Not people who are not experienced, not learning, they don't know what they're talking about Prophetﷺ when he sent Mu'adh, his Companion, he sent one of the Companions to Yemen, He said: \"you will come to People of the Scripture -Jews and Christians- He said: \"let the first thing you call them to; is WORSHIP GOD ALONE\". Once they accept that, –accept Islam, take the Shahada (Testimony of Faith), learn Tawheed (Monotheism), all of that– \"Once they do that, then tell them that there are 5prayers;\" \"that Allah has made obligatory upon them so they can learn how to pray,\" \"Once they accept that, then let them know that there is a charity that they have to get..\"", "\"Once they accept that..\". It's a gradual thing, it's a gradual process. The Prophet didn't say: \"Ô Mu'adh, when you go, let them know there's Wudu' and there's Ghusl and there is Tayammum (all are ways of Purification) And after you finish the Tayammum.. No, anything like that! because of course, you confuse the people You got to take people step by step. You got to take people gradually and individually Like you have, for example, Allah in the Quran with alcohol, there's a gradual prohibition First, Allah says (alBaqara2:219) (In it there's good and bad, and there's more bad than good) Then Allah says (anNisa4:43) (Do not come near the prayer drunk) Then Allah later says (alMaida5:90-91) –that took years– Then Allah says: (Do not drink) because people have a gradual nature So this is the thing with you, Raffaello, the gradual nation graduation?", "that you do, The gradual actions that you do is that you accept Islam, and then you take your time to learn. That's why we connect you with people, connect you with mentors, people who teach you how to pray, take you step by step gradually, and then after you learn how to pray, you start introducing prayer in your life, because now you know how to pray Then gradually learn about how to do other things. Never overwhelm yourself with so much information, So many things, you have to do this and that. It's going to just confuse you Prophetﷺ said: إِنَّ الدِّينَ يُسْرٌ (Religion is easy, and nobody goes to extreme in religion, except the religion pushes him away) You don't want religion to push you away.", "You don't want to get confused You want to take things step by step gradually. And I think you're there. I think you're ready, because of what you said so far, everything you said, I think you're there to just move forward and take that step, to accept Islam, follow the teachings that Allahﷻ sent you, gradually, step by step, And you'll have us by your side. You'll have –as you see– all of these brothers and sisters, you have Muslims generally by your side And I think that's what you should focus on.",))
