isguiding individuals.. that's one way!", "and also on top of that, the other people are saying OK there's those people who are pushing Liberalism, they're pushing Feminism and they're pushing all of these things which are against our Islamic teachings and we need to warn from those individuals and we need to warn from these things.. the issue is generally coming from those two things. And while warning people from that: is a part of our religion without a shadow of a doubt. Prophetﷺ said -as many of you already know- مَن رَأَى مِنكُم مُنْكَرًا فَلْيُغَيِّرْهُ بيَدِهِ، فإنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَبِلِسانِهِ، فإنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَبِقَلْبِهِ Who sees of you an evil deed or who sees of you a Munkar let him change it with his hand, if he cannot then with his tongue, if he cannot then to hate it with his heart So this idea of warning from Innovation or warning from Evil things or warning from people of Innovation..", "is a part of our Islamic teachings or warning from people who are pushing forwards false doctrines like Liberalism and Feminism.. which actually attacks a person's Tawheed (Monotheism) as well if you look deeply into it and into this ideology The issue is not that certain people should be warned, the issue is that the things have been happening with zero wisdom. Things have not become warning people from Innovation warning people from problems for the sake of Islam they become personal issues and if you look at many of these clips certain people talking about other people and this and that and look the purpose of this video is not to talk about any specific individual if you are in the Dawah scene and you are engaged in these things then this video concerns you I'm not talking about any specific individual I'm talking here in a general looking as a general idea and I don't want people in the comments talking about this individual and that individual", "I'll probably delete your comment or block you from the comment section this is not the purpose of this idea the purpose of this idea is to understand where the problem is coming from? The problem is not the idea of warning against people with Innovation because the Shaytaan (Satan) when he comes when he wants to cause division between the people he has to tell you you're doing good so I'm saying that the people who are doing these things they're using the Hadith of the Prophetﷺ, in their mind I know deep down they believe they're doing something which is good and Allahﷻ says in The Quran17:53 وَقُل لِّعِبَادِى يَقُولُوا۟ ٱلَّتِى هِىَ أَحْسَن ۚ (and say to My Servants to say that which is best) إِنَّ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنَ يَنزَغُ بَيْنَهُمْ (Verily The Satan he is causing enmity between each other) So yeah the way we speak has to be very balanced and has to be with wisdom.", "What is the problem now? There's two main problems: The first thing is that the idea has become a personal thing. If you watch the videos of certain individuals responding to other people \"He said that about me\" and \"he accused me of this\" and \"I accused him of this\" OK \"him\" and \"me\"! This has not become something about Islam, or warning people from Innovation, warning people from issues towards Islam and liberalism and if you make these supervisions.. I want you to go open the video and listen to yourself speaking and then think two times is your intention making this video has it become a personal issue between you and someone else?", "or are you doing this actually for the sake of Allahﷻ? the second problem with this idea is that some people think they are above criticism they think they are both correction if an individual corrects them they get very upset they get very angry and instead of responding to that specific individual in an academic way, responding to the points that he made no they would actually rather attack him and call him a traitor and this and that and call him all sorts of names -this idea of name childish name calling which we'll talk about as well- so some people are they think they are above correction from certain people because of the personal issues so I have a personal issue with you then you cannot you personally cannot correct me everyone else on the planet they can correct me but you cannot follow the command of the prophet and correct me because you are X, Y, and Z", "first thing is we need to understand what the issue of the problem is as I said first this has become a personal thing if you are a part of this problem think very deeply has this become a personal thing between you and someone else when you keep mentioning a specific individual keep mentioning his name day and night and he mentions your name day and night, you say he did this to me and I did that to him it's like little children in the playground and Daddy he hit me and Daddy hit me and then this idea of certain people not accepting criticism or Behaving Badly towards criticism so I don't want this video to be misunderstood that we shouldn't warn from certain people of innovation or certain acts of innovation so it's a way also to warn from certain acts of innovation we have to always weigh the harms and the benefits", "it's not just one from certain individual I have to have wisdom and see what is the harms and the benefits behind warning from that specific individual or perhaps I should just warn from the evil that that person is doing I just speak about the evil that the person has done instead of warning from that specific individual and the Prophetﷺ for example, he said: أقيلوا ذَوي الهيئاتِ عثَراتِهم He said: the people of good manners or good apparently or doing good then avoid like criticizing of the little things that they do don't look at their slips and then attack them on their slips, have some mercy towards your your brother and have some wisdoms to the individual privately I'm not saying you cannot speak publicly but I was talking about wisdom where is the benefit for the Muslims it's not about personal things and doing it publicly", "it's about is is it more beneficial to speak to him privately or is it more beneficial not to speak to the individual privately weighing the harms and the benefits looking at the individual perhaps you misunderstood what that person said perhaps you don't have the full image perhaps you are speaking to him speaking to him before I'm trying to give him advice and look I'm involved in the Daawah scene in the west and there are many Duaat, many many Duaat that I advise privately and I give them advice and I say to them and they give me advice and they say to me certain things OK brother you said the specific thing this specific thing is not correct we have to accept advice right people have to be given advice to one another this is not the issue yeah the issue is how we're behaving towards that criticism that is coming towards us", "Basically now we understood now where the problem is coming from. Now I want to talk about the harm effects what are the harm effects of this infighting? of this behavior that we see on social media? of this person name calling another person this person name calling this? Is this individual... and all of you know! you know very well Allahﷻ says in the Quran49:11 وَلَا تَنَابَزُوا بِالْأَلْقَابِ ۖ (Do not throw titles at one another) Then Allahﷻ says something very important, He says: بِئْسَ الِاسْمُ الْفُسُوقُ بَعْدَ الْإِيمَانِ [Verily it is an evil title to have to be called the Fasiq (a disobedient) after you were a Mu'min (Believer) just by this idea of just throwing this name calling each other every person name calling another individual] So what are the harm effects of this childish behavior that we see?", "The first thing is the image of Islam! The image of Islam publicly, The image of Islam to people who are not Muslim, the idea of the.. haters of Islam, the Islamophobs, of how they try to use these things oh this person's against.. and they make videos and reactions towards this person's spoken against this person, and then they use this as content to show they're misguided following of look how Muslims are fighting with one another! so we have the islamophobes using this content for their benefit and then we have the people who are just laymen watching and look at these people why would we..?", "I won't be a part of this just infighting people bickering with another. Why would I want to be a part of people who are not united with each other? These are the harm effects right! The harm effects also include the people confusing the masses. The Muslims. The Muslims are confused this person is speaking about this, this person's speaking about that, he's bringing some Ahadith, he's bringing some Ahadith,... Who has the truth? People are confused. They do not know what's going on. They do not know حق from باطل. That's their fault I would say initially for not seeking knowledge but it is a reality that you're confusing the people.", "Not everyone is a knowledgeable person. People watching you, listening to what you say.. it's not clear for them as you think: \"oh I've said it and I put some of these references therefore now everyone knows I'm upon the truth!\" It's not how it works. One of the major problems as well is the distrust towards the the Duaat or the Religious People, Religious figures whatever term you want to use.. People now are thinking OK this person is innovative, this person is an innovator, this person is bad, this person is bad,.. therefore what I'm gonna do now I'm not going to listen to anyone I don't know who to listen to, I'm just going to listen to myself And I've seen the harm effects that those Duaat are doing in the west.", "I get people saying some... I get reverts saying all those people are warning from each other I just pick and choose, I follow the Quran my own understanding and I take from different people who I think.. Because the person is confused now, he sees those people on the scene, they're all disagreeing with each other, he doesn't know who should he follow? and who shouldn't he follow? And also the harm effects of the infighting between the Muslims, Muslims fighting each other they've got now cheerleaders for every group Those cheerleaders are going getting videos from this person and the other cheerleaders are going getting videos from the other person They're creating channels and in these channels they post the clips about the other individual \"Oh he made this mistake\", \"oh he made that mistake\"..", "After all of this childish behavior, you're trying to come to us and convince us that what you're doing right now this childish behavior is for the sake of Allah ﷻ! If it was for the sake of Allah ﷻ you wouldn't be doing it this way. Allah ﷻ knows the intentions. I know that some people think they're sincere But look at your behavior, come back, come back, see did Shaytan deceive you in what you're doing or not! So these are the harm effects.. so what is the solution now? How do we fix this issue that we have?", "Because these issues need to be discussed, they need to be talked about And if you are a person doing Daawah in the West, you're most likely going to see this video. So if you're goint to see this video then how do we fix the issues? I'm going to give two advice, right now! One advice is for the people who are doing Daawah and one advice for people who are watching the content. Starting with the Duaat -or I don't even know if they're worthy of using that term Duaat- people who are in the west who are trying to do something for the sake of Allah ﷻ First thing, is humbling ourselves, taking the criticism from other individuals.", "There was an example for one Brother doing Daawah -I'm not going to mention his name- he was advised by another Brother Alhamdulillah he accepted the advice. He made a video, academic video, responding to the points that the other brother has made Both of them were using أخلاق, using good manners Alhamdulillah, behaving well and humbling themselves, accepting criticism, listening to the other point of view, It was done publicly! The person, he did the video about him publicly and he responded to him publicly with respect.. as someone who's got أخلاق, as a Muslim should be behaving. So that's the first thing that we need to do.", "We humble ourselves we accept criticism from other individuals and we understand that this criticism should be for the sake of Allah ﷻ The second idea is, if you want to warn, mostly try to look at the harms and the benefits and whether it's better to warn against the issue or the individual Avoid making these refutation personal. Avoid making about a specific individual, mentioning his name, calling him names. Avoid doing that because you, yourself, know very well that's not the teachings of Islam Now if you want to warn against an individual, there's another thing. A solution.", "If you want to warn against an individual, you warn against him once or twice.. or three times OK! You want to warn against the brother, warn against the brother, you want to warn against a person who you think he's an innovator, warn against the innovator Two, three times you warned against the Innovator. Alhamdulillah, Khalass, everyone who follows you now knows you believe X person is an innovator.. but to be making videos about that individual, you keep making videos, you keep making videos every couple of months, you keep coming back to the same idea and you're saying \"Oh it's just I want the people more to know that this person is an innovator..\"", "You think the people who follow you don't know? I'm sure they've watched 100 videos that you've already done. So if it's not a personal issue, you wouldn't be making this number of videos on a specific individual Now and acting with manners and good أخلاق. Wallahi this is the most important thing The person is more likely to accept your advice if you are doing this for the sake of Allah and you want that Allah ﷻ accept this as a Good Deed from you and you're doing it because you're worried about the Deen, then have good أخلاق Stop naming, calling each other..", "stop behaving like children. A lot of the people who are behaving like children -whoever you are- if you're behaving like a child, this is the Deen of Allahﷻ Your videos, what you're making on social media, has an effect on many people. Hundreds of thousands of people. It's not a game. You know! You have to act in good أخلاق, in good manners. It's not a game. Oh I want to.. I got you.. and then you scream and you go to that person, you go to this person, you try to get cameras and make noise and.. This, is it about you?", "or is it about the Deen of Allahﷻ? This would be my advice of how to solve this issue. If we humble ourselves, we act with أخلاق towards each other, someone gives Naseeha (or advice), tries to see the harms and the benefits.. If it's done publicly, then other person has been criticized publicly with good أخلاق, with evidences. Then he also responds with good أخلاق, with evidences If he's wrong, he admits he's wrong. He's not wrong, then he responds showing his evidences from the Quran and Sunnah. We don't have an issue with this idea of giving Naseeha to each other publicly, the issue is the responses and the behavior that we're using as I already mentioned.", "This is the issue. And the other solution I want to mention, it is for the people who are watching these videos. You are a huge part of this problem First the infighting between Muslims. The cheerleaders who go under everyone's post cursing this person and go to the other person, they curse this person and they start calling him names and this person calls this person names.. All of you will be accountable in the Day of Judgment. Do not think that the people who you're following are the ones who will be accountable on your behalf. You will be accountable for what you do.", "And Allahﷻ says in the Quran99:8 وَمَن يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍۢ شَرًّۭا يَرَهُۥ you know the weight of an atom! Your whole post that you type on social media is more than an atom and you will see it as Allahﷻ says it in سورة الزلزلة (Azzalzala Chapter) You will see it on the Day of Judgment in front of you These lies and those cursing and those name calling and those.. everything you're doing on social media, on the day of judgment it will be in your Saheefa (Deeds' Accounting Book) and I would prefer to have my Saheefa empty from any harming other Muslims in the day of judgment And..", "may Allahﷻ guide us. So the people, they need to stop this idea of being cheerleaders this person against this person And the second thing is, boycott those people. If a person keeps causing infighting and issues and.. just boycott them! don't watch their content.. Go watch something that is beneficial for you, especially when it is people who are responding to each other on personal issues Ya Akhi (O Brother) go learn something beneficial. Listen to teachings about the Quran and the Sunnah, Books explaining Hadith, Books explaining what you need to learn, what is going to benefit you in your Akhira (Afterlife), when you die.", "What is going to benefit you in your grave.. It's your Deeds! It's not going and liking these videos that every person is going to make towards the other person and just looking for drama and looking for fighting And.. if you love this fighting between the brothers you have a disease in your heart So, we need to humble ourselves, all of us. Starting by me, first. And we need to learn to have better أخلاق may Allahﷻ give me and give everyone listening to this video better أخلاق -and you know I'm a straightforward person- I'm just putting things how they are.", "And..if you watch this video, if you're a part of this problem, try for the sake of Allahﷻ, make Du'aa to Allahﷻ Listen to the points that I mentioned and make Du'aa to Allahﷻ is this a personal issue? now should I be continuing this childish behavior that I'm doing? Does this benefit here? outweighing the harm of what I'm doing. Is it really for the sake of Allahﷻ? or should I now move on? And focus on either the problem -talking about the problem-? or doing Daawah? or teaching people Tawheed (Monotheism)? or doing something beneficial? May Allahﷻ guide us all to The Truth. Allahumma Ameen",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"\"Dawah Drama\" A Message To Brothers Involved In Dawah! Muhammed Ali\"")
