k that you're an external person from this community or something. Don't think that people are going to look at you different because you're from a different race or a different color. Everybody you can see everybody here sitting in all different colors and races and countries and ethnicities and and we're all one family which is the family of Islam family of being a Muslim.", "So don't have that misconception. Now when it comes to other misconceptions of course that will be person dependent you know some people have some misconceptions depending on where they grew up or what they heard from other people. Another misconception is like you have to learn Arabic you know oh I have to learn Arabic to be a Muslim. No, you don't have to learn Arabic. Over 80% of Muslims have non-Arabs. They they many of them don't even know the Arabic language, right? Some only some things need to be done Arabic. Like the prayer, reciting the book of Allah because the speech of Allah, you have to recite it original language, right?", "But other than that, do you need to learn the Arabic language? Absolutely not. Is it good? Of course. But you don't need to. Another quick misconception I think you have something to say is I have to change my name if I become Muslim. You know, now people are going to start calling you uh Omar or Abu Bakr. No, you don't have to be if your name doesn't have any issues, anything against the teachings of the religion, right? Cuz mine, if my name is the servant of Jesus or something, okay, or or the slave of Jesus, no, you have a problem, right?", "Some people have these names in Arabic, Abdul Msia, for example, you have to change that name because has negative connotations, right? But if your name is just like any average name, Luke, John, this just an average name, right? You don't have you don't need to change that name. Just because you you became a Muslim, it doesn't mean that you have to change your name. Because a lot of Muslims, they will come back, oh, what's your new name in Islam? You don't have to have a new name, right? Your name that you're born with is okay so long as doesn't have any issues with it.",))
